.TH confy 1 "november 2026" "confy" "user commands"
.SH name
confy \- a config manager for linux/unix systems
.SH synopsis
.B confy
.RI [ command ]
.br
.B confy --web
.RI [ options ]
.SH description
.B confy
is a terminal user interface for tracking, grouping, previewing, editing, and rolling back configuration files. it can also manage dotfiles with git, browse remote configs over sshfs, import configs from common dotfile managers, and show activity stats and milestones.
.PP
running
.B confy
without a command opens the main interface.
.SH navigation
.TP
.B j, k
move down or up. arrow keys work too.
.TP
.B enter
open the selected file in the configured editor, or toggle the selected group.
.TP
.B space
expand or collapse a group.
.TP
.B p
toggle the live preview pane.
.TP
.B /
search tracked files and groups.
.TP
.B :
enter command mode.
.TP
.B q
quit.
.SH tui commands
enter commands by pressing
.B :
and typing the command. arguments are separated from the command name by spaces.
.SS files and backups
.TP
.B :ac
add a config file to the ungrouped group.
.TP
.BI :ac " group"
add a config file to a named group.
.TP
.B :rm
remove the selected file from confy's tracking list without deleting it from disk.
.TP
.B :l
open the last edited file.
.TP
.B :rb
restore the selected file from its latest backup.
.TP
.B :diff
compare the selected file with its retained backups. use
.B j/k
to choose a backup,
.B pgup/pgdn
to scroll, and
.B r
to restore the selected version. press
.B q
or
.B esc
to close.
.TP
.B :su
open the selected file with root privileges through
.BR pkexec (1).
.SS groups
.TP
.BI :ag " group"
create a group.
.TP
.BI :mg " group"
move the selected file to a group.
.TP
.BI :rg " group"
remove a group and move its files to ungrouped.
.SS search and sorting
.TP
.B :sort name|date|size
sort files by name, modification date, or file size.
.TP
.B :reverse
toggle ascending or descending sort order.
.TP
.B /
search files and groups as you type.
.SS themes and appearance
.TP
.BI :theme " name"
switch to a built-in or custom theme.
.TP
.B :theme
list available themes.
.TP
.B :theme list
list built-in and custom themes separately.
.TP
.B :theme new
create a custom theme with the guided wizard.
.TP
.BI :theme delete " name"
delete a custom theme.
.TP
.B :themenet
browse and download community themes.
.TP
.B :streamer
toggle streamer mode, which hides paths and timestamps.
.SS stats and imports
.TP
.B :stats
open the stats dashboard. press
.B s
to change activity sorting and
.B m
to open the milestone wall.
.TP
.B :import [chezmoi|stow|yadm]
find configs managed by chezmoi, stow, or yadm and review which ones to track. in the review, use
.B space
to toggle entries,
.B a
to select all,
.B n
to clear the selection, and
.B enter
to save.
.SS remote devices
.TP
.BI :device " host"
mount and browse a remote profile over sshfs. the host can be an ssh config alias or a user@host target.
.TP
.B :device local
return to local configs.
.TP
.B :device
show the active device or usage.
.TP
.B :ssh
alias for
.BR :device .
.SS git integration
.TP
.B :git sync
copy tracked configs into the configured dotfiles repository, organized by group.
.TP
.B :git commit
sync and commit the changes after prompting for a commit message.
.TP
.B :git push
sync, commit, and push. the repository must already have an initial commit.
.TP
.BI :git dir " path"
set the dotfiles repository path. with no path, open the path picker.
.TP
.B :git reset
reset the repository path to ~/dotfiles-git.
.TP
.B :bl
toggle the selected file or group in the git sync blacklist.
.TP
.B :bouncer
open the bulk blacklist editor. use space to toggle entries and
.B z
to confirm.
.SS configuration
.TP
.B :cd
open the config directory picker.
.TP
.BI :cd " path"
set the config directory.
.TP
.B :cd reset
reset the config directory to ~/.config.
.TP
.B :q
quit.
.SH command-line shortcuts
these compact actions run after the base
.B confy
command.
.TP
.B confy l | confy last
open the last edited file in the tui.
.TP
.BI "confy s:" text
open the tui with the search panel populated with
.IR text .
.TP
.BI "confy o:" path
track the file in ungrouped, open it, and enter the tui.
.TP
.BI "confy o:" path " g:" group
track the file in
.IR group ,
open it, and enter the tui. quote paths or group names containing spaces as needed by the shell.
.TP
.BI "confy d:" ssh-target
switch to the remote device and enter the tui.
.TP
.B confy stats
open the stats dashboard directly.
.TP
.B confy milestones
open the milestone wall directly.
.TP
.B confy import [chezmoi|stow|yadm]
open the import review directly.
.TP
.B confy hooks
open the hooks configuration in the configured editor.
.TP
.B confy st:share
print copyable markdown stats and exit.
.TP
.B confy st:img[:transparent]
write a themed svg stats image.
.TP
.B confy st:banner[:transparent]
write a wide themed svg stats image.
.TP
.B confy st:post[:transparent]
write a portrait themed svg stats image.
.TP
.BI "to:" path
append this argument to an image command to choose its output path. by default, confy writes confy-stats-img.svg, confy-stats-banner.svg, or confy-stats-post.svg in the current directory. transparent images add -transparent before the .svg extension.
.TP
.B confy completions bash|elvish|fish|powershell|zsh
print a shell completion script to standard output.
.TP
.B confy h | help | man
display usage information and exit.
.TP
.B confy v | ver | version | e | edition
display version information and exit.
.TP
.B confy --help, confy --version
display help or version information and exit.
.SH web editor
.B confy --web
starts the browser editor. without launch flags, confy interactively asks for gui or text mode, bind address, port, and optional password.
.PP
the gui mode provides a browser-based grouped file interface. text mode provides a terminal-style browser with vim-like editing. both modes edit tracked files and create backups before writing.
.TP
.BI --ip " address"
set the bind address. the alias
.B --bind
is also accepted.
.TP
.BI --port " port"
set the listening port.
.TP
.B --gui
select gui mode.
.TP
.B --text
select text mode.
.TP
.BI --mode " gui|text"
select a mode.
.TP
.BI --password " password"
set a web password.
.TP
.B --no-password
disable the web password.
.TP
.B -ni, --no-interactive
skip setup prompts and use defaults: gui mode, 127.0.0.1, port 3000, no password.
.TP
.B --help
show web editor usage.
.PP
the built-in web server uses http. use a tls reverse proxy when serving it beyond localhost.
.SH hooks
hooks are configured separately in
.IR ~/.config/confy/hooks.toml .
the file contains a
.B [hooks]
table with arrays of shell commands for these events:
.BR opened ,
.BR changed ,
.BR rolled_back ,
.BR restored ,
.BR tracked ,
and
.BR untracked .
commands run asynchronously through
.BR sh (1)
as the current user. each receives the
.B CONFY_EVENT
and
.B CONFY_FILE
environment variables. restoring a backup from
.B :diff
fires both the
.B rolled_back
and
.B restored
events.
.PP
example:
.nf
[hooks]
opened = []
changed = ["notify-send 'confy' \"$CONFY_FILE changed\""]
rolled_back = []
restored = []
tracked = []
untracked = []
.fi
.SH files
.TP
.I ~/.config/confy/config.toml
main configuration and tracked file data.
.TP
.I ~/.config/confy/hooks.toml
event hook commands.
.TP
.I ~/.config/confy/themes/
custom theme files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/confy/backups/
compressed backups used by rollback and the diff browser. confy retains up to three backups per tracked file.
.SH dependencies
the core interface has no runtime dependencies beyond the system terminal. remote profiles require
.BR sshfs (1),
elevated editing requires
.BR pkexec (1),
and git operations require
.BR git (1).
remote elevated editing may also require
.B user_allow_other
in
.IR /etc/fuse.conf .
.SH see also
.BR sshfs (1),
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR git (1)
